        <type>void</type>
        <definition>void csmp::ThermalConvectionETHZ_Example::thermalEquilibrationAtSectorIntegrationPoints</definition>
        <argsstring>(Model&lt; 3U &gt; &amp;, Region&lt; 3U &gt; &amp;, H2OLookup &amp;)</argsstring>
        <name>thermalEquilibrationAtSectorIntegrationPoints</name>
        <qualifiedname>csmp::ThermalConvectionETHZ_Example::thermalEquilibrationAtSectorIntegrationPoints</qualifiedname>
        <param>
          <type><ref refid="classcsmp_1_1_model" kindref="compound">Model</ref>&lt; 3U &gt; &amp;</type>
          <defname>model</defname>
        </param>
        <param>
          <type><ref refid="classcsmp_1_1_region" kindref="compound">Region</ref>&lt; 3U &gt; &amp;</type>
          <defname>ref</defname>
        </param>
        <param>
          <type><ref refid="classcsmp_1_1_h2_o_lookup" kindref="compound">H2OLookup</ref> &amp;</type>
          <defname>water</defname>
        </param>
        <briefdescription>
<para>calculation of new density liquid and enthalpy in FV sectors </para>
        </briefdescription>
        <detaileddescription>
<para>Computes nodal heat source/sink by equilibrating the transported fluid mass/enthalpy by means of fluid-rock equilibration.</para>
<para><orderedlist>
<listitem><para>the transported heat is distributed over the FV sectors</para>
</listitem><listitem><para>the fluid properties are recomputed at each sector integration point</para>
</listitem><listitem><para>the heating / cooling is computed sector by sector</para>
</listitem></orderedlist>
</para>
<para>4.</para>
<para>X. Also computes new finite volume &quot;enthalpy content liquid&quot; from sector contents</para>
<para>Following a transport step, the total enthalpy on the node needs to be distributed between rock and fluid such that these are in thermal equilibrium.</para>
<para><simplesect kind="attention"><para>this method is concerned only with the computation of specific rather than volume-integrated quantities. </para>
</simplesect>
</para>
        </detaileddescription>
        <inbodydescription>
        </inbodydescription>
        <location file="examples/source/ThermalConvectionETHZ_Example.h" line="38" column="8" bodyfile="examples/source/ThermalConvectionETHZ_Example.cpp" bodystart="810" bodyend="991"/>
      </memberdef>
