        <type>void</type>
        <definition>void csmp::ThermalConvectionETHZ_Example::nodalSourceOperands</definition>
        <argsstring>(Model&lt; 3U &gt; &amp;, Region&lt; 3U &gt; &amp;, H2OLookup &amp;, const double &amp;time_increment)</argsstring>
        <name>nodalSourceOperands</name>
        <qualifiedname>csmp::ThermalConvectionETHZ_Example::nodalSourceOperands</qualifiedname>
        <param>
          <type><ref refid="classcsmp_1_1_model" kindref="compound">Model</ref>&lt; 3U &gt; &amp;</type>
          <defname>model</defname>
        </param>
        <param>
          <type><ref refid="classcsmp_1_1_region" kindref="compound">Region</ref>&lt; 3U &gt; &amp;</type>
          <defname>ref</defname>
        </param>
        <param>
          <type><ref refid="classcsmp_1_1_h2_o_lookup" kindref="compound">H2OLookup</ref> &amp;</type>
          <defname>water</defname>
        </param>
        <param>
          <type>const double &amp;</type>
          <declname>time_increment</declname>
        </param>
        <briefdescription>
<para>nodal source-sink terms due to density amd energy content changes upon thermal equilibration </para>
        </briefdescription>
        <detaileddescription>
<para>computes nodal source-sink terms due to changes in the density and energy content of the fluid following (as are established during the thermal equilibration step)</para>
<para>Effective terms at the nodes were already computed in thermal equilibrate so that these do not need to be repeated here</para>
<para>The &apos;nodal fluid volume source&apos; is a total (integrated) point source, which is calculated from the difference in the density liquid (actual fluid density at onset of transport step) and the &apos;fluid density&apos; calculated after the enthalpy transport step. </para>
        </detaileddescription>
        <inbodydescription>
        </inbodydescription>
